From a9735b22446fcaff50ec3473758171a29378e255 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Codex handoff (Claude)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:54:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Operator API: MCP server with OAuth for Claude, read tools
 and gated write tools

Group HQ now speaks the Model Context Protocol at /mcp so a claude.ai custom
connector, Claude Desktop or Claude Code can read the dashboard, CRM, people,
mentees, grants, LAPS, property deals, webinars and non-secret settings as a
named admin. An OAuth 2.1 server (dynamic registration, PKCE S256, consent page
behind the admin login) issues stateless HMAC-signed tokens for claude.ai; a
static bearer serves Claude Code and Desktop. Five CRM write tools go through
app.services.campaigns exactly as /crm does and are offered only while
GHQ_OPERATOR_WRITES is "enabled". Mounted only when a credential is validly set;
rotating GHQ_OPERATOR_OAUTH_SECRET signs every connector out. Three DB-free unit
checks cover the tokens, the OAuth flow and the MCP handshake and gate;
docs/operator-api.md has the setup, tool list and limits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LReXhJakn8pa2r1EHjVsaE
